course: dictionary
lesson: 13300
title: Words made of smaller words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller words joined together, and the parts can show you what the whole word means. Gravedigger is made of grave and digger. A grave is a hole where a dead person is buried, and a digger is someone who digs, so a gravedigger is someone who digs graves.
explain: Check the words around it. «The gravedigger dug a deep hole in the cemetery.» The cemetery is the place, the hole is the grave, and digging is the job. That fits exactly with the meaning.
explain: Sometimes the word is used in a figurative way, which paints a picture rather than naming a real person. «The new rule was the gravedigger of the club's old games.» No one dug a real hole. The rule brought an end to the old games, so the word means something that ends something.
fact: A gravedigger is a person whose job is to dig graves in a cemetery.
fact: Graves are dug so that the dead can be buried.
fact: «Gravedigger» is a noun, and its plural is gravediggers.
fact: «Gravedigger» can also mean someone or something that brings about the end of something.
fact: A word made of two smaller words joined together is called a compound word, and gravedigger is one.
exercise: «The gravedigger dug the hole in the cemetery.» Who dug the hole? | *A gravedigger | A doctor | A postman | A gardener with a rose bed
exercise: Which two smaller words are joined to make gravedigger? | cem and etery | *grave and digger | grav and edger | gate and dig
exercise: Which tool would a gravedigger use to dig a grave? | *A spade | A kettle | A bicycle | A paintbrush
test: What does a gravedigger do? | Drives a bus to the sea | Sells flowers in a shop | *Digs graves for burying the dead | Looks after lost dogs
test: Which is the plural of gravedigger? | *gravediggers | graveddiggers | gravedigs | gravediggies
exam: In «The new rule was the gravedigger of the club's old games», what does gravedigger mean? | A friendly neighbour | A tool for digging gardens | *Something that brings about the end of something | A person who digs graves
